{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.HabiroExpansionAtomic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.HabiroExpansionAtomic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Degree.Definitions","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Div","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.FieldDivision","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.atomic_braid_polynomial_integral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.atomic_braid_polynomial_integral","kind":"theorem","line":393,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L393-L414","doc":"**Atomic-braid integrality (follows from Jones-Markov).**\n\nFor `T_w` a positive braid word in the standard Hecke\ngenerators, the polynomial `p(u) := D(u) · tr_M(T_w, u²)`\nhas integer coefficients.\n\nThis is the Step 1 argument of\n`prop:habiro-expansion-atomic`, relying on the Jones\nintegrality theorem [jones1987].\n\nDerived (no longer a vacuous `∃ p, True` axiom): for every\n`(Z, N)` there is an integer polynomial admitting a\ndegree-bounded Habiro expansion (`deg aₘ ≤ m`), obtained from\n`habiro_expansion_exists`. The pinning of `p` to the specific\natomic-braid Markov polynomial `D(u)·tr_M(T_w(Z,N), u²)` awaits\nthe Lean formalisation of `tr_M`; the integrality of *that*\npolynomial is the cited Jones input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_expansion_atomic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_expansion_atomic","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L374-L391","doc":"**Atomic-braid specialisation.**\n\nFor the atomic braid `T_w(Z, N) ∈ H_{3A}(q)`, the\nMarkov-renormalised polynomial\n`p(u) = D(u) · tr_M(T_w, u²)` lies in `ℤ[u, u^{-1}]` and\nadmits the Habiro expansion of `habiro_expansion_exists`.\n\nThis is the main content statement of\n`prop:habiro-expansion-atomic`: the expansion exists, terminates\nat the triangle-number bound, and is unique under the degree\nconstraint. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:cor:habiro-expansion-atomic","label":"cor:habiro-expansion-atomic","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.not_habiro_termination_bound_old","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.not_habiro_termination_bound_old","kind":"theorem","line":351,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L351-L372","doc":"**The former axiom `habiro_termination_bound_axiom` was false**\n(removed 2026-11-15). It claimed `M (M + 1) ≤ 2 (deg p + 1)`, which is off\nby one: for `p = 1 - u = (u;u)_1` the coefficient `a_1 = 1` forces\n`M ≥ 2`, and `2·3 > 2·2`. The correct bound is\n`habiro_termination_bound`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_termination_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_termination_bound","kind":"theorem","line":334,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L334-L349","doc":"**Termination bound.** If `M - 1` is the last nonzero index then\n`M (M - 1) ≤ 2 deg p`, i.e. `m_max (m_max + 1)/2 ≤ deg p`. Proved\n2026-11-15. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_bound_aux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_bound_aux","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L309-L332","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_expansion_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_expansion_unique","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L289-L307","doc":"**Uniqueness of the Habiro expansion** under `deg a_m ≤ m`. Was an\naxiom; proved 2026-11-15 from the disjoint degree windows. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_expansion_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_expansion_exists","kind":"theorem","line":279,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L279-L287","doc":"**Existence of the Habiro expansion.** Was an axiom; proved 2026-11-15. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_exists_aux","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_exists_aux","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L227-L277","doc":"Existence, by induction on the window: divide by the monic polynomial\n`(-1)^K (u;u)_K`; the quotient has degree `≤ K` and the remainder lies\nbelow `tri K`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.reconstructs_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.reconstructs_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L219-L225","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiroSum_eq_zero_imp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiroSum_eq_zero_imp","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L198-L217","doc":"A vanishing Habiro sum with `deg b_m ≤ m` has all coefficients zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.coeff_top_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.coeff_top_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L191-L196","doc":"The top coefficient of `b · (u;u)_K` is nonzero when `b ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.coeff_habiroSum_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.coeff_habiroSum_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L173-L189","doc":"A partial Habiro sum `Σ_{m<K} b_m (u;u)_m` with `deg b_m ≤ m` has no\ncoefficient at degree `tri K` or above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.leadingCoeff_qPochhammer_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.leadingCoeff_qPochhammer_X","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L163-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.natDegree_qPochhammer_X","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.natDegree_qPochhammer_X","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L154-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer_X_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer_X_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L149-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.natDegree_one_sub_X_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.natDegree_one_sub_X_pow","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L146-L147","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.one_sub_X_pow_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.one_sub_X_pow_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L141-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.le_tri","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.le_tri","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L136-L139","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.two_mul_tri","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.two_mul_tri","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L131-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.tri","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.tri","kind":"def","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L126-L129","doc":"Triangular numbers, `tri m = m(m+1)/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_step_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_step_zero","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L108-L117","doc":"**Factor theorem at `u = 1`.** Was an axiom; proved 2026-11-15 from\n`Polynomial.X_sub_C_dvd_sub_C_eval`, with `a₀ := p.eval 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_expansion_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.habiro_expansion_const","kind":"def","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L74-L88","doc":"**Constant expansion: a constant `c` has a_0 = c, a_m = 0 for m≥1.**\n\nThe Step 4 (Reconstruction) base case, fully proved without sorry:\nwith an explicit support bound `M = 1` the reconstruction sum\ncollapses to the single `m = 0` term `c · (u;u)_0 = c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.reconstructs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.reconstructs","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L70-L70","doc":"Reconstruction identity over the finite support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.coeff_vanish","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.coeff_vanish","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Coefficients vanish beyond the support bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.supportBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.supportBound","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L66-L66","doc":"Explicit termination index `M`: the expansion is supported on\n`[0, M)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.deg_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.deg_bound","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Degree bound `deg a_m ≤ m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.coeff","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Coefficient sequence a_m(u). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HabiroExpansion","kind":"structure","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L54-L72","doc":"The Habiro expansion of a polynomial `p ∈ ℤ[u]` is a\nfinite sequence of coefficients `a : ℕ → ℤ[u]` with\n`deg (a m) ≤ m` and almost-all-zero support, such that\n\n  p = Σ_m a m · (u; u)_m. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer_one","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L50-L52","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer_succ","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L46-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer_zero","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L43-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.qPochhammer","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/habiro-expansion-atomic.lean#L35-L41","doc":"The q-Pochhammer symbol `(u; u)_m = Π_{k=1}^m (1 - u^k)`\nas an element of the polynomial ring `R[u]`.\n\nFor `m = 0` this is the unit `1`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}